## Best Practices

### 1. Proper Cleanup

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT: Clean up map on destroy
ngOnDestroy(): void {
  if (this.map) {
    this.map.remove();
    this.map = null;
  }
}
```

### 2. Use Signals for Reactive State

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT: Reactive layer visibility
layers = signal<MapLayer[]>([]);
visibleLayers = computed(() => this.layers().filter(l => l.visible));
```

### 3. Lazy Load Map Data

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT: Load data based on map bounds
this.map.on('moveend', () => {
  const bounds = this.map!.getBounds();
  this.loadDataInBounds(bounds);
});
```

### 4. Error Handling

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT: Handle map errors
this.mapService.getSites().subscribe({
  next: (sites) => this.addMarkers(sites),
  error: (error) => {
    console.error('Failed to load sites', error);
    this.errorSignal.set('Failed to load map data');
  }
});
```

